    "description": "2.8-inch 320x240 ILI9341 on SPI2, lying landscape; a resistive XPT2046 touch on SPI3 (one finger); sound the chip's own 8-bit DAC on GPIO26 through the board's amplifier; the BOOT button; the microSD slot wired to pins no host is left for (spi3 is the touch's): kept as data for the program",
    "notes": [
        "One product page sells three kinds of this board with the same pins: ILI9341, ILI9341 with another init sequence, ST7789. This data was tried with the ILI9341 driver of DGX.",
        "The reset of the panel is wired to EN: no GPIO resets it alone.",
        "CN1 carries GPIO27 and GPIO22, the pair for an I2C module. The schematic V0.1 shows no net on its contact 3, the board has GPIO22 there.",
        "P3 carries GPIO22 too, beside GPIO21, which is the backlight, and GPIO35, which is input only."
    ],
    "mcu": {
        "target": "esp32",
        "part": "ESP32-D0WD-V3",
        "flash_mb": 4,
        "notes": "the ESP32 has two SPI hosts for the program: SPI2 the display, SPI3 the touch; the SD slot's pins (23, 19, 18, cs 5) have no host left and are data only (buses.sdspi.sd)"
    },
